# hub-control topology — ELN overlay over the substrate settings-sync plane.
#
# Includes the substrate `settings-sync` topology (settings:consumer →
# settings-sync fans out per spoke, plus the six-axis remote_* geometry pushes) and
# layers on the ELN-only pieces: the discovery-collector fan-out and the three
# application-key pushes (rules, log_memory, flush_every_line). The
# `num_partitions = 1` pin must live here — frontmatter is read from the
# top-level file only, so the included file's `var` is skipped.

var num_partitions = 1

include settings-sync

make_node Discovery_Collector discovery-collector 300
make_node Vault_Group settings HTTP_Out spoke
make_node Null null

# discovery-collector fans `discovery.get` to every spoke on its own 300s tick
# and union-merges the replies into the hub options. Its replies come back
# through `settings`, a Vault_Group over the same Vault group `spoke` as
# `firehose` in aggregator.tsl: one HTTP_Out per member, following the Vault on
# reload. That egress admits only DECLARED destinations, so it needs
# `allow_replies_to discovery-collector` beside the settings-sync declaration
# or the discovery replies are dropped; both are declared ONCE, on the group,
# and replayed to every member present now or built later. Never hand-wire a
# second HTTP_Out for a spoke already in the group beside it: two egresses
# both minting from the same session double the pushes a spoke receives.
command_node settings-sync:config add_setting newspack_event_logger_nodes_rules performance newspack_event_logger_nodes_rules
command_node settings-sync:config add_setting newspack_event_logger_nodes_log_memory performance newspack_event_logger_nodes_log_memory
command_node settings-sync:config add_setting newspack_event_logger_nodes_flush_every_line performance newspack_event_logger_nodes_flush_every_line
command_node settings:config allow_replies_to settings-sync
command_node settings:config allow_replies_to discovery-collector

connect_node settings-sync settings
connect_node discovery-collector settings
connect_node settings null

secure
